# `a2a whatsnew`: renders the embedded release-notes corpus — no space, no
# config needed. This shared t3 test binary is built with -X
# main.version=0.1.0 (main_test.go), which predates every versioned entry in
# the real corpus. The selected release range is therefore empty, while the
# independently loaded current known-issues list must still be present in text
# and JSON. Rich rendering (digest text, impact ordering, action-scope
# directives, JSON shape) is covered by
# internal/cli/cmd_whatsnew_test.go and internal/mcp/tools_whatsnew_test.go
# against a fixed, injected corpus.
exec a2a whatsnew
stdout 'KNOWN ISSUE'
stdout 'The macOS companion remains ad-hoc signed'

exec a2a whatsnew --since 0.1.0
stdout 'KNOWN ISSUE'
stdout 'The macOS companion remains ad-hoc signed'

exec a2a whatsnew --since 0.1.0 --json
stdout '"id": "KI-MACOS-ADHOC-SIGNING"'
